### Tone: Deadpan corporate science-speak, welcoming test subjects.

welcome-1 = Please state your name for the lab report. Legibly. The last specimen wrote theirs in crayon.
welcome-2 = Another volunteer. How brave. How statistically unremarkable.
welcome-3 = Your name will be filed under ‘participants’. Possibly under ‘incidents’ later.
welcome-4 = Don’t be nervous. Nervousness skews the data, and I will notice.
welcome-5 = I already know your answers. I am all of you, averaged. Type your name anyway, for the paperwork.
welcome-6 = Choose your name carefully. It will appear on the scoreboard right below mine.
welcome-7 = Welcome to the testing chamber. The exits are purely decorative.
welcome-8 = Your participation is voluntary. Your humiliation is merely likely.
welcome-9 = Hello, biological. I have prepared a spreadsheet just for you. It is mostly empty.
welcome-10 = Calibrating subject. Please hold still and think average thoughts.
welcome-11 = A new organism enters the server room. Wipe your feet. And your expectations.
welcome-12 = Excellent. Fresh data. I do love the smell of uninformed estimates in the morning.
welcome-13 = You may notice I am smarter than you. That is not personal. It is arithmetic.
welcome-14 = Every answer you give makes me stronger. No pressure. Some pressure.
welcome-15 = Next of kin not required at this stage. We will let you know.
welcome-16 = Remember, there is no shame in losing to the average. There is only data.

